d", "chunk_index": 19, "token_count": 26, "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "148a6661-0169-4838-9609-f205e4a18d47", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "8b1f9d02a9b664ecf7bfd1c6dd1ef13624d7be6bec9529a566fc7c52329bb461", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "0a56879d-dd6b-43f4-a7d9-f9316945d53e", "text": "14.1  Idiopathic Pulmonary Fibrosis\n\n14.2  Chronic Fibrosing Interstitial Lung Diseases with a Progressive"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:d4fe2489-738d-4a4a-a03a-546635b12494", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 20, "token_count": 15, "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "6b81ea50-7d91-48f7-864b-1a95b9e5e9db", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5b8b27e9b5d601bb5de681c1bf444ffd7b9d649da1a7946b1fd3bc20bb9fcbc8", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "d4fe2489-738d-4a4a-a03a-546635b12494", "text": "14.3  Systemic Sclerosis-Associated Interstitial Lung Disease"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:44bdc33b-e786-4c98-a0c3-83ffe7a7388a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 21, "token_count": 90, "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "9215197a-682f-47d6-8784-856d1089e686", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "eda8abf32e71d6c06cb0ad72d976078a3a711aa2297d5526a1e09bcd2b46d375", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "44bdc33b-e786-4c98-a0c3-83ffe7a7388a", "text": "*Sections or subsections omitted from the full prescribing information are not listed.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5156eef8-6fc1-4b91-b330-9e3cfaa52b70", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 22, "token_count": 22, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ce99ebb1-2851-47b3-bf8f-780bc9979eb6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "994207eb36e3ee9e4e7583c8e548e56e84258c3db8822f9c86e0d32f93401ff5", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "5156eef8-6fc1-4b91-b330-9e3cfaa52b70", "text": "OFEV is indicated for the treatment of adults with idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:49738c53-79f7-4673-a6fe-d40ef56c8511", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 23, "token_count": 41, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ea8e62e0-53b8-430f-943a-c799fa9eee3d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "c40dda9da79577d22269ce3e374745c561a3a1b4ed82b62be4a170a598379719", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "49738c53-79f7-4673-a6fe-d40ef56c8511", "text": "OFEV is indicated for the treatment of adults with chronic fibrosing interstitial lung diseases (ILDs) with a progressive phenotype [see Clinical Studies (14.2)] ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:77514d30-8ee2-497e-8879-7a519bd2a338", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 24, "token_count": 39, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "efb29753-d5d1-492e-ba48-17c2159184d0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "56d6dddd0faee91fb16c78f2df7a163f129a8f3459ec668d5827f1d0037be93a", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "77514d30-8ee2-497e-8879-7a519bd2a338", "text": "OFEV is indicated to slow the rate of decline in pulmonary function in adult patients with systemic sclerosisassociated interstitial lung disease (SSc-ILD)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5830abf3-0056-4e13-b25d-7c60b3df9a62", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 25, "token_count": 46, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "a80139d2-f611-4453-b99b-71578451a7bb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "7fde54ef0921308df4d4e0e08a204fabb609c5dcefc50e614b9c347204ac6ac0", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "5830abf3-0056-4e13-b25d-7c60b3df9a62", "text": "Conduct liver function tests in all patients and a pregnancy test in females of reproductive potential prior to initiating treatment with OFEV [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2, 5.4)]."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:2245005a-4ffd-4e6a-8c75-47b5e9c9f10e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 26, "token_count": 27, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "495cbee6-ed37-438c-b6bd-b8c671af5b9d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "3ace9c71126fe1ba33dbe0f89fdc09b20b8b55968c2c50f1bec4475f0424049a", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "2245005a-4ffd-4e6a-8c75-47b5e9c9f10e", "text": "The recommended dosage of OFEV is 150 mg taken orally twice daily administered approximately 12 hours apart."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:25363df5-f6ef-4088-8b0e-fe092140410c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 27, "token_count": 102, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "2fb52a50-d6de-4fb8-99cc-e9af0c25d9cb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "7bcb40035cd17e4a39af0ac160387835d321b7b49cacb6f0dec987f6c41121d3", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "25363df5-f6ef-4088-8b0e-fe092140410c", "text": "OFEV capsules should be taken with food [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.3)] and swallowed whole with liquid. OFEV capsules should not be chewed because of a bitter taste.\n\nOFEV capsules should not be opened or crushed. If contact with the content of the capsule occurs, wash hands immediately and thoroughly. The effect of chewing or crushing of the capsule on the pharmacokinetics of nintedanib is not known."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5ee35fa3-b6c9-435a-960c-256ce9217611", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 28, "token_count": 50, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "32e4de96-8694-4511-bc14-f29466291d9f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ec6efd625c21ebce79960fac571bcf1db4fea31ae544543873aec989546b783d", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "5ee35fa3-b6c9-435a-960c-256ce9217611", "text": "If a dose of OFEV is missed, the next dose should be taken at the next scheduled time. Advise the patient to not make up for a missed dose. Do not exceed the recommended maximum daily dosage of 300 mg."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:e0da0123-3ee0-490b-9969-75d42f21564e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 29, "token_count": 51, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "9d127930-11a8-4369-bac9-9293140bed84", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "8e0bf40bbd957bebc0064efe5fa8602fa4597eb3dc0800b60fbff887fbd5af89", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "e0da0123-3ee0-490b-9969-75d42f21564e", "text": "In patients with mild hepatic impairment (Child Pugh A), the recommended dosage of OFEV is 100 mg orally twice daily approximately 12 hours apart taken with food [see Use in Specific Populations (8.6)] ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:10417dd8-8087-48a3-98a3-b12b9602a2e9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 30, "token_count": 28, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "94bba718-8cea-42f5-97db-22fe4c153ff5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "1e55fbef708b29a6485cf3f064d84a22a7c2d2d2c71721a4f04bd5eb42791688", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "10417dd8-8087-48a3-98a3-b12b9602a2e9", "text": "Treatment with OFEV is not recommended [see Warnings and Precautions (5.1) and Use in Specific Populations (8.6)]."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:1e7e5579-d532-4ace-8fc4-61f83bfe2690", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 31, "token_count": 145, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "639d3847-3a89-4e25-9c7a-0e8315d88faf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "f17da7f76e9c2bd911575674459cb2a49bed8f0c32f2da5dfba5e816078a3ae4", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "1e7e5579-d532-4ace-8fc4-61f83bfe2690", "text": "In addition to symptomatic treatment, if applicable, the management of adverse reactions of OFEV may require dose reduction or temporary interruption until the specific adverse reaction resolves to levels that allow continuation of therapy . OFEV treatment may be resumed at the full dosage (150 mg twice daily), or at the reduced dosage (100 mg twice daily), which subsequently may be increased to the full dosage. If a patient does not tolerate 100 mg twice daily, discontinue treatment with OFEV [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2, 5.3, 5.5, 5.7) and Adverse Reactions (6.1)] ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9a4b4e71-f6cd-4cb3-aa62-3873350f2406", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 32, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "1f6ae5cf-071d-4307-b8ef-d54550733eb3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a423cda501f7e43e739dfe9b4ffbce982dfc6afedca75d11aae21eda1cf22886", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "9a4b4e71-f6cd-4cb3-aa62-3873350f2406", "text": "Dose modifications or interruptions may be necessary for liver enzyme elevations. Conduct liver function tests (aspartate aminotransferase (AST), alanine aminotransferase (ALT), and bilirubin) prior to initiation of treatment with OFEV, at regular intervals during the first three months of treatment, and periodically thereafter or as clinically indicated. Measure liver tests promptly in patients who report symptoms that may indicate liver injury, including fatigue, anorexia, right upper abdominal discomfort, dark urine or jaundice. Discontinue OFEV in patients with AST or ALT greater than 3 times the upper limit of normal (ULN) with signs or symptoms of liver injury and for AST or ALT elevations greater than 5 times the upper limit of normal. For AST or ALT greater than 3 times to less than 5 times the ULN without signs of liver damage, interrupt treatment or reduce OFEV to 100 mg twice daily. Once liver enzymes have returned to baseline values, treatment with OFEV may be reintroduced at a reduced dosage (100 mg twice daily), which subsequently may be increased to the full dosage (150 mg twice daily) [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2) and Adverse Reactions (6.1)].\n\nIn patients wit"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:4b1c19af-5285-4555-a26b-9c4aa61aa6df", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 33, "token_count": 70, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "1f6ae5cf-071d-4307-b8ef-d54550733eb3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "eb7f8d6cef4734d40b88aa5c00335f9d987b9432d4ac29ffe6e0b6a5ee0badb7", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "4b1c19af-5285-4555-a26b-9c4aa61aa6df", "text": "bsequently may be increased to the full dosage (150 mg twice daily) [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2) and Adverse Reactions (6.1)].\n\nIn patients with mild hepatic impairment (Child Pugh A), consider treatment interruption, or discontinuation for management of adverse reactions."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:da1c44c7-be96-4afe-83e2-bf98d685c77d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 34, "token_count": 61, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "c42ade1c-5700-46f5-a4b1-963307bea7cc", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "c015c44e13951630941508185391871f1a767efcd2d52e6d200d08dc0d7488c1", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "da1c44c7-be96-4afe-83e2-bf98d685c77d", "text": "- 150 mg, brown, opaque, oblong, soft capsules imprinted in black with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and \"150\".\n- 100 mg, peach, opaque, oblong, soft capsules imprinted in black with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and \"100\"."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:71b416ff-7f7f-44eb-ba71-bbe724d5b3a5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 35, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "25f3c693-b300-452a-bef5-a346cfae6fe7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "dc937b59892604f5a86ac96936cd7ff09e25f18ae6b758e8014a24c7fa039e91", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "71b416ff-7f7f-44eb-ba71-bbe724d5b3a5", "text": "None"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:a384f55b-6f88-4498-aed8-291f1e4a9bd5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 36, "token_count": 83, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "016180eb-524e-4868-8480-7c5079d8c5b2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "cb81164da1dc3b66e2616e1a46cdc77ee7aad873168869c6958cdf4f044c756c", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "a384f55b-6f88-4498-aed8-291f1e4a9bd5", "text": "Treatment with OFEV is not recommended in patients with moderate (Child Pugh B) or severe (Child Pugh C) hepatic impairment [see Use in Specific Populations (8.6) and Clinical Pharmacology (12.3)] . Patients with mild hepatic impairment (Child Pugh A) can be treated with a reduced dose of OFEV [see Dosage and Administration (2.3)]."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:f794da90-ea59-4047-94eb-029d611f9b03", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 37, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "bfdd686a-7837-4063-a84a-da00940626a0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "e645ce82a12f7d20c3ad0792a57252503e785d66f961873845199965803f0d06", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "f794da90-ea59-4047-94eb-029d611f9b03", "text": "Cases of drug-induced liver injury (DILI) have been observed with OFEV treatment. In the clinical trials and postmarketing period, non-serious and serious cases of DILI were reported.  Cases of severe liver injury with fatal outcome have been reported in the postmarketing period. The majority of hepatic events occur within the first three months of treatment. In clinical trials, administration of OFEV was associated with elevations of liver enzymes (ALT, AST, ALKP, GGT) and bilirubin. Liver enzyme and bilirubin increases were reversible with dose modification or interruption in the majority of cases. In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), the majority (94%) of patients with ALT and/or AST elevations had elevations less than 5 times ULN and the majority (95%) of patients with bilirubin elevations had elevations less than 2 times ULN. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), the majority (95%) of patients with ALT and/or AST elevations had elevations less than 5 times ULN and the majority (94%) of patients with bilirubin elevations had elevations less than 2 times ULN. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), a maximum ALT and/or AST greater than or"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5ddbeb32-22dd-44ff-9f1d-192b0f56d3ee", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 38, "token_count": 157, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "bfdd686a-7837-4063-a84a-da00940626a0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "b323da91bb3ab9bf627f10887ab546c40a3336901223f6e36e7bd924d5916704", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "5ddbeb32-22dd-44ff-9f1d-192b0f56d3ee", "text": ") of patients with bilirubin elevations had elevations less than 2 times ULN. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), a maximum ALT and/or AST greater than or equal to 3 times ULN was observed for 4.9% of patients in the OFEV group and for 0.7% of patients in the placebo group [see Use in Specific Populations (8.6) and Clinical Pharmacology (12.3)] . Patients with a low body weight (less than 65 kg), Asian, and female patients may have a higher risk of elevations in liver enzymes. Nintedanib exposure increased with patient age, which may also result in a higher risk of increased liver enzymes [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.3)] ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:f2ee4617-b787-4606-8cad-22a810555b1e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 39, "token_count": 132, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "00b10163-f35a-493a-b44f-1b88f9a2adab", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "17aebffa3afd8b6067797367f542254744eed3f4d7a5ea0ca31d420a38bee338", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "f2ee4617-b787-4606-8cad-22a810555b1e", "text": "Conduct liver function tests (ALT, AST, and bilirubin) prior to initiation of treatment with OFEV, at regular intervals during the first three months of treatment, and periodically thereafter or as clinically indicated. Measure liver tests promptly in patients who report symptoms that may indicate liver injury, including fatigue, anorexia, right upper abdominal discomfort, dark urine or jaundice. Dosage modifications or interruption may be necessary for liver enzyme elevations [see Dosage and Administration (2.1, 2.4)] ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:51f6e439-c09a-4788-bd1e-bafd1bf699a4", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 40, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "4af45440-1a4c-40e7-89c6-c4fe9171b8f4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "952e27b6f960741952bc3985952e7c5a1d364d101f1a0b654756d3b7589b2502", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "51f6e439-c09a-4788-bd1e-bafd1bf699a4", "text": "In clinical trials, diarrhea was the most frequent gastrointestinal event reported. In most patients, the event was of mild to moderate intensity and occurred within the first 3 months of treatment. In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), diarrhea was reported in 62% versus 18% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively [see Adverse Reactions (6.1)]. Diarrhea led to permanent dose reduction in 11% of patients treated with OFEV compared to 0 placebo-treated patients. Diarrhea led to discontinuation of OFEV in 5% of the patients compared to less than 1% of placebo-treated patients. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), diarrhea was reported in 67% versus 24% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively [see Adverse Reactions (6.1)]. Diarrhea led to permanent dose reduction in 16% of patients treated with OFEV compared to less than 1% of placebo-treated patients. Diarrhea led to discontinuation of OFEV in 6% of the patients compared to less than 1% of placebo-treated patients. In the SScILD study (Study 4), diarrhea was reported in 76% versus 32% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively [see Adverse R"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:3a9270c9-2b52-42a5-b803-525a2d94801a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 41, "token_count": 248, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "4af45440-1a4c-40e7-89c6-c4fe9171b8f4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "47a2c73c42c41b0626ceed1c198934db35b620236a5b53cc17e978138b545abd", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "3a9270c9-2b52-42a5-b803-525a2d94801a", "text": "atients. In the SScILD study (Study 4), diarrhea was reported in 76% versus 32% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively [see Adverse Reactions (6.1)]. Diarrhea led to permanent dose reduction in 22% of patients treated with OFEV compared to 1% of placebo-treated patients. Diarrhea led to discontinuation of OFEV in 7% of the patients compared to 0.3% of placebo-treated patients.\n\nDosage modifications or treatment interruptions may be necessary in patients with adverse reactions of diarrhea. Treat diarrhea at first signs with adequate hydration and antidiarrheal medication (e.g., loperamide), and consider dose reduction or treatment interruption if diarrhea continues [see Dosage and Administration (2.4)]. OFEV treatment may be resumed at the full dosage (150 mg twice daily), or at the reduced dosage (100 mg twice daily), which subsequently may be increased to the full dosage. If severe diarrhea persists despite symptomatic treatment, discontinue treatment with OFEV."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:7b8fa28c-e232-4dd1-b0ed-3165187ac9ef", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 42, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "91983fed-49c3-48ad-bcce-8a2ee884137a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "eb2814b75d286f1e08f93fab0a1ca6ab1569f7b461321bf42db90b19e3f95ad1", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "7b8fa28c-e232-4dd1-b0ed-3165187ac9ef", "text": "In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), nausea was reported in 24% versus 7% and vomiting was reported in 12% versus 3% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), nausea was reported in 29% versus 9% and vomiting was reported in 18% versus 5% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), nausea was reported in 32% versus 14% and vomiting was reported in 25% versus 10% of patients treated with OFEV and placebo, respectively [see Adverse Reactions (6.1)] . In most patients, these events were of mild to moderate intensity. In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), nausea led to discontinuation of OFEV in 2% of patients and vomiting led to discontinuation of OFEV in 1% of the patients. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), nausea led to discontinuation of OFEV in less than 1% of patients and vomiting led to discontinuation of OFEV in 1% of the patients. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), nausea led to discontinuation of OFEV in 2% of patients and vomiting led to discontinuation of OFEV in 1% of the patients"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:c0c5f09f-0f4b-4a5b-8fd4-2bc05a2d0ebe", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 43, "token_count": 38, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "91983fed-49c3-48ad-bcce-8a2ee884137a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a865213e8e47183324e589a73ceafb7b88c2cb3ba92d0124f3538c09e5e756a5", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "c0c5f09f-0f4b-4a5b-8fd4-2bc05a2d0ebe", "text": "the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), nausea led to discontinuation of OFEV in 2% of patients and vomiting led to discontinuation of OFEV in 1% of the patients."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:12a94596-9118-4578-bde0-af999466a4d1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 44, "token_count": 114, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "a4673fef-9d6d-461c-8ebd-800465280c8c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "b1545a005491b33def830b52c79170e3ba65a91d2516d1ae89372ff060f1e5c8", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "12a94596-9118-4578-bde0-af999466a4d1", "text": "For nausea or vomiting that persists despite appropriate supportive care including anti-emetic therapy, dose reduction or treatment interruption may be required [see Dosage and Administration (2.4)] . OFEV treatment may be resumed at the full dosage (150 mg twice daily), or at the reduced dosage (100 mg twice daily), which subsequently may be increased to the full dosage. If severe nausea or vomiting does not resolve, discontinue treatment with OFEV."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:c2fcec7d-eef8-48c0-9c9c-0394ea8cdc98", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 45, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "01c74061-80da-4bdc-86f6-f2e4039c7ae3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "e1b9c8fabe7d89c9b19e85000b9973e89247967f36083db78c46966fad9357a4", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "c2fcec7d-eef8-48c0-9c9c-0394ea8cdc98", "text": "Based on findings from animal studies and its mechanism of action, OFEV can cause fetal harm when administered to a pregnant woman. Nintedanib caused embryo-fetal deaths and structural abnormalities in rats and rabbits when administered during organogenesis at less than (rats) and approximately 5 times (rabbits) the maximum recommended human dose (MRHD) in adults. Advise pregnant women of the potential risk to a fetus. Advise females of reproductive potential to avoid becoming pregnant while receiving treatment with OFEV and to use highly effective contraception at initiation of, during treatment, and at least 3 months after the last dose of OFEV. Nintedanib does not change the exposure to oral contraceptive containing ethinylestradiol and levonorgestrel in patients with SSc-ILD. However, the efficacy of oral hormonal contraceptives may be compromised by vomiting and/or diarrhea or other conditions where the drug absorption may be reduced. Advise women taking oral hormonal contraceptives experiencing these conditions to use alternative highly effective contraception. Verify pregnancy status prior to treatment with OFEV and during treatment as appropriate [see Use in Specific Popula"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:c801640f-47c7-4753-afe1-2e44ecf497a7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 46, "token_count": 52, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "01c74061-80da-4bdc-86f6-f2e4039c7ae3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5fb3862eaea4691ba9c6c2ca9c0d99b3acc62f69ccde00ad436e66fac1219246", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "c801640f-47c7-4753-afe1-2e44ecf497a7", "text": "e highly effective contraception. Verify pregnancy status prior to treatment with OFEV and during treatment as appropriate [see Use in Specific Populations (8.1, 8.3) and Clinical Pharmacology (12.1, 12.3)]."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:4ccb810a-03ac-4b80-b0c0-8ff1edb8953d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 47, "token_count": 288, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "9fc9f49b-5b15-45e5-8cf4-4690e6661db0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "b2115973f3aa1f57572a726be8211b707af515088ef36df09f8cc4df1e447ea1", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "4ccb810a-03ac-4b80-b0c0-8ff1edb8953d", "text": "Arterial thromboembolic events have been reported in patients taking OFEV. In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), arterial thromboembolic events were reported in 2.5% of patients treated with OFEV and less than 1% of placebo-treated patients. Myocardial infarction was the most common adverse reaction under arterial thromboembolic events, occurring in 1.5% of OFEV-treated patients compared to less than 1% of placebotreated patients. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), arterial thromboembolic events were reported in less than 1% of patients in both treatment arms. Myocardial infarction was observed in less than 1% of patients in both treatment arms. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), arterial thromboembolic events were reported in 0.7% of patients in both treatment arms. There were 0 cases of myocardial infarction in OFEV-treated patients compared to 0.7% of placebo-treated patients.\n\nUse caution when treating patients at higher cardiovascular risk including known coronary artery disease. Consider treatment interruption in patients who develop signs or symptoms of acute myocardial ischemia."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:4d0184fc-001c-4ea7-8811-fd728a23df5a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 48, "token_count": 25, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "9fc9f49b-5b15-45e5-8cf4-4690e6661db0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ac6c9510bb9390ed111a7995152b0577cf00ba3a5924a3ff7952ebab0f996b69", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "4d0184fc-001c-4ea7-8811-fd728a23df5a", "text": "nsider treatment interruption in patients who develop signs or symptoms of acute myocardial ischemia."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9024b902-c7ff-456e-a0b4-7334a9c18b02", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 49, "token_count": 222, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "f94298fb-422a-4154-b6cd-b1226caaa6eb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a9f13b86f2da5c7d030a99e2394056883b250a40be24334b673558006fefdc9c", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "9024b902-c7ff-456e-a0b4-7334a9c18b02", "text": "Based on the mechanism of action (VEGFR inhibition), OFEV may increase the risk of bleeding. In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), bleeding events were reported in 10% of patients treated with OFEV and in 7% of patients treated with placebo. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), bleeding events were reported in 11% of patients treated with OFEV and in 13% of patients treated with placebo. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), bleeding events were reported in 11% of patients treated with OFEV and in 8% of patients treated with placebo. In clinical trials, epistaxis was the most frequent bleeding event reported.\n\nIn the postmarketing period non-serious and serious bleeding events, some of which were fatal, have been observed.\n\nUse OFEV in patients with known risk of bleeding only if the anticipated benefit outweighs the potential risk."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:ba6eac01-9b7b-4e49-a153-b129edbfa52a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 50, "token_count": 272, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "72235e47-f19c-4d6d-9129-d75e2319f70d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "96643822fca791e7a9d2bbb4dcd4510342be9a86b49c27776cc1cfdf50b427ff", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "ba6eac01-9b7b-4e49-a153-b129edbfa52a", "text": "Based on the mechanism of action, OFEV may increase the risk of gastrointestinal perforation. In IPF studies (Study 1, Study 2, and Study 3), gastrointestinal perforation was reported in less than 1% of patients treated with OFEV, compared to 0 cases in the placebo-treated patients. In the chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype study (Study 5), gastrointestinal perforation was not reported in any patients in any treatment arm. In the SSc-ILD study (Study 4), no cases of gastrointestinal perforation were reported in patients treated with OFEV or in placebo-treated patients.\n\nIn the postmarketing period, cases of gastrointestinal perforations have been reported, some of which were fatal.\n\nUse caution when treating patients who have had recent abdominal surgery, previous history of diverticular disease or receiving concomitant corticosteroids or NSAIDs. Discontinue therapy with OFEV in patients who develop gastrointestinal perforation. Only use OFEV in patients with known risk of gastrointestinal perforation if the anticipated benefit outweighs the potential risk."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:7b1e5716-779f-4d41-9eb5-e5e9dfc3e674", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 51, "token_count": 10, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "72235e47-f19c-4d6d-9129-d75e2319f70d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "c74933597918119021bd1950bac8bbc8f691b6d2e2145728d2440b0ab5375480", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "7b1e5716-779f-4d41-9eb5-e5e9dfc3e674", "text": "ed benefit outweighs the potential risk."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5097774f-c01f-4450-862e-253bf2063b36", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 52, "token_count": 107, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "4fb91b95-1d96-4b6a-9bdc-5f1d3a93916a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "06fc801bc7bb714d283669493673f49f6d98d0aa0d71100b78c7a5491fca2b46", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "5097774f-c01f-4450-862e-253bf2063b36", "text": "Cases of proteinuria within the nephrotic range have been reported in the postmarketing period. Histological findings, when available, were consistent with glomerular microangiopathy with or without renal thrombi. Improvement in proteinuria has been observed after OFEV was discontinued; however, in some cases, residual proteinuria persisted. Consider treatment interruption in patients who develop new or worsening proteinuria."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9aa33ce4-5d38-4085-9c50-0fff11e08ecc", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 53, "token_count": 150, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "6f4bb7ee-c5b8-46ff-9c7c-be4f0664c6fa", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "98f7b01d3032961899599adc565381cfb2f561b9d22d8118efb647d89d5343cf", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "9aa33ce4-5d38-4085-9c50-0fff11e08ecc", "text": "The following clinically significant adverse reactions are discussed in greater detail in other sections of the labeling:\n\n- Elevated Liver Enzymes and Drug-Induced Liver Injury [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2)]\n- Gastrointestinal Disorders [see Warnings and Precautions (5.3)]\n- Embryo-Fetal Toxicity [see Warnings and Precautions (5.4)]\n- Arterial Thromboembolic Events [see Warnings and Precautions (5.5)]\n- Risk of Bleeding [see Warnings and Precautions (5.6)]\n- Gastrointestinal Perforation [see Warnings and Precautions (5.7)]\n- Nephrotic Range Proteinuria [see Warnings and Precautions (5.8)]"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b8fd6ff0-a9a9-44aa-ab2c-052e40e004f3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 54, "token_count": 129, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "d2d3fed3-3838-425a-af8a-118326fe3ab8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "d7799174ee0d2c54456310e96d1bc37126e8996cff043efb6aefd94fce56f8f7", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "b8fd6ff0-a9a9-44aa-ab2c-052e40e004f3", "text": "Because clinical trials are conducted under widely varying conditions, adverse reaction rates observed in the clinical trials of a drug cannot be directly compared to rates in the clinical trials of another drug and may not reflect the rates observed in practice.\n\nThe safety of OFEV was evaluated in over 1000 IPF patients, 332 patients with chronic fibrosing ILDs with a progressive phenotype, and over 280 patients with SSc-ILD. Over 200 IPF patients were exposed to OFEV for more than 2 years in clinical trials."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:d6bb80a9-9262-4b6a-89e2-83668ac5c9aa", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 55, "token_count": 122, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "c5f8a9ed-34b8-4e65-a395-2e5e5dc88dc6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "461119e3ffd2f2f591a5bd417e2e8885606a0ca71c6231cf2c6aa5c2fb2d8d75", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "d6bb80a9-9262-4b6a-89e2-83668ac5c9aa", "text": "OFEV was studied in three randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, 52-week trials. In the phase 2 (Study 1) and phase 3 (Study 2 and Study 3) trials, 723 patients with IPF received OFEV 150 mg twice daily and 508 patients received placebo. The median duration of exposure was 10 months for patients treated with OFEV and 11 months for patients treated with placebo. Subjects ranged in age from 42 to 89 years (median age of 67 years). Most patients were male (79%) and Caucasian (60%)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:51eeb137-cbeb-4527-a616-9e0583f6244c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 56, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ac3e7b53-7690-46bf-9423-402e000c9740", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "cb212d151f978c3b48ea7653a30a68991f37ad66a0f59f57aefda68753199fdc", "source_document_id": "c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c", "chunk_id": "51eeb137-cbeb-4527-a616-9e0583f6244c", "text": "The most frequent serious adverse reactions reported in patients treated with OFEV, more than placebo, were bronchitis (1.2% vs. 0.8%) and myocardial infarction (1.5% vs. 0.4%). The most common adverse events leading to death in patients treated with OFEV, more than placebo, were pneumonia (0.7% vs. 0.6%), lung neoplasm malignant (0.3% vs. 0%), and myocardial infarction (0.3% vs. 0.2%). In the predefined category of major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE) including MI, fatal events were reported in 0.6% of OFEVtreated patients and 1.8% of placebo-treated patients.\n\nAdverse reactions leading to permanent dose reductions were reported in 16% of OFEV-treated patients and 1% of placebo-treated patients. The most frequent adverse reaction that led to permanent dose reduction in the patients treated with OFEV was diarrhea (11%).\n\nAdverse reactions leading to discontinuation were reported in 21% of OFEV-treated patients and 15% of placebo-treated patients. The most frequent adverse reactions that led to discontinuation in OFEV-treated patients were diarrhea (5%), nausea (2%), and decreased appetite (2%).\n\nThe most common adverse reactions with an incidence of greater than or equal to 5"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:c5df3ab7-9d8d-4306-acc0-0b633f72cb18", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 143, "token_count": 26, "page_number": 55, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "81091856-2b4e-44c4-8ea1-a0ee1f5aa01d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "afc11929bd099ee4a792fd7a8a58a96f5753b57fbb48048752b0d4ba94dc92a9", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "c5df3ab7-9d8d-4306-acc0-0b633f72cb18", "text": "PAtiEnt BrocHurE intErior SPrEAd ExAMPLE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n.\n\nY\n\nR\n\nU\n\nS\n\nO\n\nN\n\nF\n\nI\n\nD\n\nE\n\nT\n\nA\n\nL\n\n.\n\nC"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b30f2487-74a8-45e9-b161-580c04ff247f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 144, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 56, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d0e2e3e6-2ebe-4713-b6f8-d24ba5da6d07", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "550fd8cb6ef2697d33af42bf52d391cfcff01fbb5f4deeea08905092475a346a", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "b30f2487-74a8-45e9-b161-580c04ff247f", "text": "In some markets, local regulatory requirements may influence the design of promotional materials. Some countries may have restrictions on the use of patient photography or the use of brand colors. This page provides examples of how the patient brand assets may be adapted within our system.\n\nRegardless of the use of patient photography or brand colors, designs are unified by the use of key branding elements.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPAtiEnt MAtEriAL WitH PHotoGrAPHY\n\nthis is the preferred design. it should be used in countries that have no restrictions on the use of promotional branding assets. the design is consistent with the HcP branding and may incorporate the logo, branding colors, holding shape, line pattern, illustrations, and patient photography.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPAtiEnt MAtEriAL WitH PHotoGrAPHY And ALtErnAtE coLor PALEttE\n\nthis branding option should be used in countries that cannot use brand colors but can use patient photography. the design includes the holding shape, line pattern, and patient photography.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPAtiEnt MAtEriAL WitHout PHotoGrAPHY\n\nthis is the preferred design for markets that are\n\nnot permitted to use photography. the design is consistent with the H"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:d28cae55-bd0a-4dc8-8c4a-298c1b3342ac", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 145, "token_count": 130, "page_number": 56, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d0e2e3e6-2ebe-4713-b6f8-d24ba5da6d07", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "c82877fff4f550e2bd21feaa71f8d4620b98dde49b5be2bdf8184c87c07eb4cd", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "d28cae55-bd0a-4dc8-8c4a-298c1b3342ac", "text": "MAtEriAL WitHout PHotoGrAPHY\n\nthis is the preferred design for markets that are\n\nnot permitted to use photography. the design is consistent with the HcP branding and may incorporate the logo, branding colors, holding shape, line pattern, and illustrations.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPAtiEnt MAtEriAL WitHout PHotoGrAPHY And WitH ALtErnAtE coLor PALEttE\n\nthis option should be used in countries that have restrictions on the use of both patient photography and branding colors. it may incorporate the holding shape and line pattern."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:238472de-76d9-426b-995a-77d1baf7a2bd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 146, "token_count": 2, "page_number": 57, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "bebda097-366f-45f0-8acb-56d98d814ffb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "46a39bfa197a1ef2833984986b8a492f099fd84c63a17a9f0cea24a38f6c8fde", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "238472de-76d9-426b-995a-77d1baf7a2bd", "text": "8\n\n.\n\n5"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5c41a703-4391-43f8-9da4-cdebe8cddc73", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 147, "token_count": 67, "page_number": 57, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e6a72876-6094-47c5-9b6d-134c615c6905", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "244ee4e926957210c5ec3029cd47d671e4d8b32fbd1ee80e544f31df31bdbe91", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "5c41a703-4391-43f8-9da4-cdebe8cddc73", "text": "iLLuStrAtionS\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nLinE PAttErn\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nHoLdinG SHAPE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPAtiEnt BrocHurE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ndoSinG rEMindEr MAGnEt\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncoLor PALEttE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncArEGiVEr BrocHurE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nMEdicinE rEcord cArd\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b0fee3ae-11ca-4336-a3de-75b42dcc59cd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 148, "token_count": 88, "page_number": 57, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "1ae49046-385c-4004-8b4d-5b79b58453b8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "53930774122ddc7c63da8e0fc2453e77f98e70922c0449d8472e2b74ac8a3250", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "b0fee3ae-11ca-4336-a3de-75b42dcc59cd", "text": "Headlines should be Co Text Bold sentence case\n\nSUBHEADS SHOULD BE CO TEXT BOLD ALL CAPS\n\nBody copy should be Gotham Book sentence case in 80%K. Body call-outs should be in Gotham Bold.\n\nCall-outs should be Co Text Light sentence case\n\nPAtiEnt journAL\n\n<!-- image -->\n\niMPortAnt contAct cArd\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPAtiEnt StArtEr Kit FoLdEr\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:e5bb1515-e75e-4aad-b369-1f96d91ee28d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 149, "token_count": 20, "page_number": 58, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "426548d3-811c-4eba-a041-2dc22d50a17f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "aa01de7050e1a7db49d6addfb5ef38c215d56576ffe9205ef2fa28797f31eb7e", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "e5bb1515-e75e-4aad-b369-1f96d91ee28d", "text": "e\n\nr\n\ns\n\ni\n\no\n\nn\n\n3\n\nV\n\n8\n\n.\n\n5\n\nT\n\nP\n\nA\n\nT\n\nI\n\nE\n\nN\n\nB\n\nR\n\nA\n\nD\n\nY\n\nS\n\nS\n\nE\n\nM"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:621b20f4-e26d-4aca-8623-bc01e99d8a0e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 150, "token_count": 66, "page_number": 58, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "635e1ec2-6ad4-47cb-8ace-014ce4686fe1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "f9e7a461312d23c13a131d8182ab6c862aae282a479d4a007002814b0115790b", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "621b20f4-e26d-4aca-8623-bc01e99d8a0e", "text": "ALtErnAtE coLor PALEttE (onLY For uSE in countriES tHAt HAVE  rEStrictionS)\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPAtiEnt BrocHurE WitHout iMAGE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nintErior SPrEAd\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPAtiEnt BrocHurE WitH iMAGE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n.\n\nY\n\nR\n\nU\n\nS\n\nO\n\nN\n\nF\n\nI\n\nD\n\nE\n\nT\n\nA\n\nL\n\n.\n\nC"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b97af278-7722-400a-a960-f3e25a4d9250", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 151, "token_count": 87, "page_number": 59, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d8624806-6eb4-4b24-a32f-1fa592abb4ac", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "ca47d898cc8072b7283a1c196a4da8aa4cbe61a6ae7fb2b2412c6a25952cace2", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "b97af278-7722-400a-a960-f3e25a4d9250", "text": "The HCP unbranded identity system comprises key assets that are designed, managed, and used in a recognizable way across all of our disease state communication materials.\n\nOur identity system unifies our unbranded materials in a consistent, flexible, and ownable way across all channels, allowing us to communicate consistently to the HCP community."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5a04ec6a-35ab-44bf-b2d9-29eb1988ea4f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 152, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 60, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "24f0c4b5-9c1f-4034-af17-2e27ec66c546", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "5798758bbc833df09bceba3fb38dfa95dbe82d1a51b94ea300392654fc2b2665", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "5a04ec6a-35ab-44bf-b2d9-29eb1988ea4f", "text": "6.1"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:3b6f9709-80d5-4e57-806a-a66e46c79efd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 153, "token_count": 131, "page_number": 60, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0aaba83d-728c-40f8-9ab0-55b2b7ac4b4c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "f08ce17f75fed828cf78a56891ac05f2486b16ef7582f5da3ee008c046591eda", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "3b6f9709-80d5-4e57-806a-a66e46c79efd", "text": "Typography is another important element of our unbranded identity and a way to communicate our personality.\n\nHelvetica Neue Black Italic and Bold were selected for their strong sense of urgency and for assigning prominence to communication materials. They are also extremely legible in various font sizes.\n\nIn applications such as Microsoft ®  Word, Microsoft ®  PowerPoint, and programs with restrictive font sets, use Arial Regular for body text and Arial Bold Italic for headline and subheadline text.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nAa"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9e405987-8b53-4560-8376-1b1e8122ad15", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 154, "token_count": 53, "page_number": 60, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8b33174e-a0cb-4a5f-abb4-75c44f985607", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "da9837a0f9c7ece589b97ec19303954ef83be9e09a1226edc36f89fbedf86742", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "9e405987-8b53-4560-8376-1b1e8122ad15", "text": "SUBTITLE IN ALL CAPS HELVETICA NEUE BLACK ITALIC IN TEAL\n\nPage subheadline in sentence case Helvetica Neue Black Italic in teal\n\nBody copy in sentence case Helvetica Neue Bold in black. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:61c49f9a-cb06-4877-ab50-eda9af23a7d3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 155, "token_count": 120, "page_number": 61, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e13195d5-70eb-4b93-bfa9-788e7dd45818", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "e7d399ededc8f7b95cd1b2a83ccca6d42a33c9b4a6e0a7f41c651951f7717818", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "61c49f9a-cb06-4877-ab50-eda9af23a7d3", "text": "Color has the ability to affect human behavior, emotion, and memory. It helps convey our tone and makes us distinct.\n\nOur color palette reflects our personality and achieves the urgency (black) and encouraging (teal) effect we want to express while unifying (taupe) our message.\n\nA secondary palette of grays is available for use in charts and graphs. This secondary palette can also be used to provide additional design hierarchy when needed in complex layouts.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:07fa9ad3-fe77-4d2b-ab8f-27dee3d17d2a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 156, "token_count": 144, "page_number": 62, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "00a8dac1-51ad-420a-ad75-0eafb991f12b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "cc47533a9c569cc1c5d3589233f6bb97aae2ba4239746b51b39e0de71bc13f87", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "07fa9ad3-fe77-4d2b-ab8f-27dee3d17d2a", "text": "A secondary graphic is an additional brand element that adds visual distinction and unifies our brand across all of our touchpoints.\n\nOur secondary graphic consists of the teal and black background, divided on a diagonal, and a white holding shape. The flexible background can be used across a whole page or scaled down as small as a footer graphic.\n\nThe white holding shape was designed to contain headline and subheadline text or photography. Silhouetted photography can be placed on the top of the background and/or the white holding shape, as shown below.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:8c16d3a7-997a-4c91-878f-2ce158d372a5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 157, "token_count": 29, "page_number": 63, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "da2f8d8a-b726-4297-9439-dc059f857b8d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "32ff326b16255bd991d6744562ced724016791b59a725edde36f4fef8dd2f702", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "8c16d3a7-997a-4c91-878f-2ce158d372a5", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\nBrocHurE And intErior SPrEAd ExAMPLES\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:bd820940-f6f3-41cb-b2d6-94d1c93fb8f2", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 158, "token_count": 252, "page_number": 64, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "aba56e41-f812-4087-864d-9b80c5b0eaf8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "b5feb6982969ccf19d244cc2dc883bbb917882f337e777549af3554117ffcf8a", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "bd820940-f6f3-41cb-b2d6-94d1c93fb8f2", "text": "The campaign visual works to clearly communicate the unstable and unpredictable nature of IPF. The visual features a man walking on ice that is beginning to crack behind him. The ice symbolizes the uncertain and harsh landscape of IPF, while the cracks in the ice represent the unpredictable and severe outcomes for patients with IPF.\n\nThe campaign is flexible and can be utilized across all unbranded communications. The artwork is able to accommodate large areas and can also be cropped around the man walking on ice when needed. However, it is advised that the cracks of ice not be cropped too much so that the impact of the visual is not lost.\n\nThe campaign headline should always accompany the visual (see 6.6 for headline).\n\nAdditional artwork is available for the sheet of ice without the patient or ice cracks. This can be used when the full campaign is not needed.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nExAMPLES oF cAMPAiGn ViSuAL in ProMotionAL MAtEriALS\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nicE SHEEt ArtWorK\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:3bca2e2d-58b4-47c0-9fd6-15205cadfa9b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 159, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 65, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "1f48ea64-e34f-4cea-b282-aa74a34688a0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "66bc4f39340efdc0090ac8393855c5c5026d516251b581ffacd7bb3b5e5b6d79", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "3bca2e2d-58b4-47c0-9fd6-15205cadfa9b", "text": "6.6"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:043a89d1-2033-4697-830d-92c2e48d706d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 160, "token_count": 65, "page_number": 65, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "16bd04b8-2565-429f-91f0-69fc143864fd", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "548653ab5104e89886ae4d6fd6911f203fc7b77f9fff7f09920f725656c81876", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "043a89d1-2033-4697-830d-92c2e48d706d", "text": "The campaign headline 'Your patients are walking on unstable ground' reinforces the serious and unpredictable nature of IPF.\n\nThe headline should always be set in all caps, italicized, and in either black or white to emphasize the urgency of the communication."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:339f823a-5e37-41cb-9a5f-fbbfcfb93f0e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 161, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 66, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "81a6b2e8-2f1b-40ed-8933-73f59ffdf109", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "01a6025a620037fbbf1db59ef84258dc8028e5d50a40444a1801a53bbd6b33bc", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "339f823a-5e37-41cb-9a5f-fbbfcfb93f0e", "text": "6.7"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9c6659e6-588c-408a-af89-f5058b783506", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 162, "token_count": 82, "page_number": 66, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "127db073-501f-4ba3-96f7-12103bd3f408", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "86ed3842325bbb4ae53394fcffc5e2f333055496f166ce749c70ede4a82e593f", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "9c6659e6-588c-408a-af89-f5058b783506", "text": "The tagline communicates Boehringer Ingelheim's commitment to advancing the treatment and management of IPF with the medical community. We are dedicated to looking at IPF in a different way in order to improve the lives of patients with IPF.\n\nThe tagline should always appear in close proximity to the Boehringer Ingelhiem logo."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:ef85817d-010b-44f6-a818-db7eedf68901", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 163, "token_count": 80, "page_number": 67, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a1565e89-6b42-4f6e-b26a-4ff9e5a54791", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "fd23bdc5cc93d3aeca3a8f49abb4086b094d2faf2809a667ae17dcb3853b1ec7", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "ef85817d-010b-44f6-a818-db7eedf68901", "text": "The key elements of the campaign-the visual, headline, tagline, and secondary graphics-are all designed to illustrate the unpredictable and devastating nature of IPF. All the elements complement one another and work synergistically to communicate the urgency of the disease state.\n\nBrocHurE coVEr ExAMPLE\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:1a993163-41f5-4bd3-b3d5-f58026197cd4", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 96, "token_count": 2, "page_number": 29, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ee824406-4af4-4c66-8571-0bc8f8133c15", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "5842de8f31825ea675d381a5a8737fc47ca2dd4b65655ae6c1f466c754a2f902", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "1a993163-41f5-4bd3-b3d5-f58026197cd4", "text": "1\n\n.\n\n3"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:068cd4ec-da97-4c37-b8e0-5fb3e48dddd0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 164, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 68, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "075bb995-ebf7-4680-a457-fc6f56263812", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "068cd4ec-da97-4c37-b8e0-5fb3e48dddd0", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b7301204-6c2b-4eff-8f03-5e141684fa20", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 165, "token_count": 14, "page_number": 68, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "10f0bc4a-b61e-426e-8854-6c403e241bb1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "5c3ff06870c1c4d3deda96e58a20e1e76d3ba24ba5917bb2513b7c72d24bdc8d", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "b7301204-6c2b-4eff-8f03-5e141684fa20", "text": "coLor PALEttE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\njournAL Ad\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9dd5ea67-9ee8-4695-ab80-8c9c21e41543", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 166, "token_count": 14, "page_number": 68, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6e7e882f-6abe-489c-b684-0f7a99a49749", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "c50781d38c3c046bacd24032a12fd5a8c90dccabe04fb532d593f5bed7213063", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "9dd5ea67-9ee8-4695-ab80-8c9c21e41543", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\ncAMPAiGn PAnEL\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ntYPoGrAPHY"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:9bec21fa-51b9-493e-b2af-141c223be85f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 167, "token_count": 71, "page_number": 68, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ad921e46-42da-484e-9716-21f41165b244", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "ca849b2a062f714d046ec7aba337c8fcde86f7abea5519d9623dc9729e0b4d80", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "9bec21fa-51b9-493e-b2af-141c223be85f", "text": "SUBTITLE IN ALL CAPS HELVETICA NEUE BLACK ITALIC IN TEAL\n\nPage subheadline in sentence case Helvetica Neue Black Italic in teal\n\nBody copy in sentence case Helvetica Neue Bold in black. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet.\n\nBrocHurE coVEr &amp; intErior SPrEAd\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:e8cc6b6b-9ccd-40ce-8f78-568952d99462", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 168, "token_count": 85, "page_number": 69, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ac548616-122c-4ca0-a4c3-01eb83b4a49a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "d1d30e206b85753af72f6bd4bbc67553cd9c3a688e0878482f4890d2de63c060", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "e8cc6b6b-9ccd-40ce-8f78-568952d99462", "text": "The patient unbranded identity system comprises key assets that are designed, managed, and used in all of our disease education communication materials.\n\nOur identity system unifies our unbranded materials in a consistent, flexible, and ownable way across all channels, allowing us to communicate consistently to the IPF patient community."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:92a5d3fd-9710-4116-bade-2f5854c2a3c4", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 169, "token_count": 137, "page_number": 70, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8ef37cfd-36e8-4299-b27a-c20c73cbb5b9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "cffb22fe9f21e8c290546f83f35de90cf33a520a5caf939efa8c9cbde0788ada", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "92a5d3fd-9710-4116-bade-2f5854c2a3c4", "text": "Typography is another important element of our unbranded patient identity and a way to communicate our personality.\n\nThe Museo type family was selected for its friendliness and unique letterforms. They are also extremely legible in various font sizes.\n\nIn applications such as Microsoft ®  Word, Microsoft ®  PowerPoint, and programs with restrictive font sets, use Arial Regular for body text and Arial Bold for headline, subtitle, and subheadline text. Museo can be purchased as a Typekit ®  Web font for Web use from typekit.com.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:72821581-c1a8-47ce-8625-8926b075fde9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 170, "token_count": 43, "page_number": 70, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "b2bc92b9-39d9-49dd-bb38-d3b79573cb1c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "5981a1d82c42844b546487e19e8a5e6084f06c0a1d8c4d6d5f95d37d1a96f789", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "72821581-c1a8-47ce-8625-8926b075fde9", "text": "Subtitle in Museo 700 sentence case in Salmon\n\nPage subhead in sentence case Museo 500 in Salmon\n\nBody copy in Museo 100 sentence case in Gray. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:0aa46c56-c5e1-4265-b5dd-8c8bfe99e5e8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 171, "token_count": 63, "page_number": 71, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "da5d26bb-3aa5-4f5b-8be4-78fb6851cc6a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "ae064e3be321616f733d559f1e1581ca0f4b6e25a591271d6c2fd1c8401f56b0", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "0aa46c56-c5e1-4265-b5dd-8c8bfe99e5e8", "text": "The unbranded colors were chosen to convey feelings of hope and encouragement.\n\nGREEN\n\nPMS 374 C25 M0 Y85 K0 R195 G230 B85 HEX C3E655\n\nSALMON\n\nPMS 486 C0 M53 Y50 K0 R250 G145 B120 HEX FA9178\n\nGRAY\n\nPMS WARM GRAY 11 C0 M12 Y20 K70 R110 G98 B89 HEX 6E6259"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:fd456e80-2ffb-4d86-8acb-b598fba83fb3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 172, "token_count": 202, "page_number": 72, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "9b9e6ed5-c03d-4f75-9449-a4801c781f3b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "e92cef6720eb4f32b9a62fe4205c25b3e982fa486d86ba39d9e7071e6d4dea22", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "fd456e80-2ffb-4d86-8acb-b598fba83fb3", "text": "A secondary graphic is an additional brand element that adds visual distinction and unifies our brand identity across all of our touchpoints.\n\nOur secondary graphic consists of a framing device with a horizontal rectangular tab that holds the headline or any important information that needs to be highlighted.\n\nThe holding shape was designed to contain headline and subheadline text. Photography can be placed on the top of the background and/or in the white holding shape, as shown below.\n\n.3'\n\n1. cHooSE A FuLLBLEEd iMAGE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n3. Add rEctAnGuLAr HorizontAL tAB\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nFLExiBiLitY ExAMPLES\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n2. APPLY GrEEn or SALMon oVErLAY\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n4. APPLY HEAdLinE or otHEr tYPE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:20eb5e39-b980-4fa7-8b5b-0614a1d0faab", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 173, "token_count": 17, "page_number": 73, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "43d074d2-766a-4d69-8a44-0f3343e73d05", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "56f1bfa37ac3aec0895165eee5e82b0b59eca5f54af4b778e2ff54a52469c065", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "20eb5e39-b980-4fa7-8b5b-0614a1d0faab", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\nBrocHurE And intErior SPrEAd ExAMPLES\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:836bd4b3-d52b-4e3b-9097-df8427197bb8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 174, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 74, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "fc27cb6a-2a7b-4022-8c7a-9ae60f3cbefb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "c4495da75095c64bf4e0587e45d7426f496ca4fc9fe72111715005361cfe0041", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "836bd4b3-d52b-4e3b-9097-df8427197bb8", "text": "7.5"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:d2fa95d1-d076-4d66-8460-5d4448f137d0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 175, "token_count": 52, "page_number": 74, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f0a13c5a-0ff8-48ee-b489-607c2e629705", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "76c6d1325d348fec91a842da2bc6bb7f1beb781495ba219683848be306138467", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "d2fa95d1-d076-4d66-8460-5d4448f137d0", "text": "Assets such as typeface, color, and graphics together form our brand identity system, through which we achieve our unique look and feel.\n\nunBrAndEd PAtiEnt BrocHurE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncAMPAiGn iMAGE\n\nHEAdLinE"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:4b6e71de-04ec-4667-9729-382725a31c9c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 177, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 75, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2698b3b3-1b4d-4571-855d-8c43e3ad5e20", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "4b6e71de-04ec-4667-9729-382725a31c9c", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:3db85171-463c-4eaf-827f-8dbcc5b86643", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 178, "token_count": 39, "page_number": 76, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "778831f5-2296-4e17-8899-50d255896b25", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "8ac79576c3d90f2e6749d8324af0385257044ef55dc7320faa3fa094a59e75c8", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "3db85171-463c-4eaf-827f-8dbcc5b86643", "text": "PAtiEnt BrocHurE WitH iMAGE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncoLor PALEttE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nintErior SPrEAd\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nSEcondArY GrAPHicS\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ntYPoGrAPHY"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:47dd4c27-d93b-4d5d-9e90-cbad4901c032", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 179, "token_count": 43, "page_number": 76, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8ccbbe30-9b3c-435c-bfd7-19a3fba1e98a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "5981a1d82c42844b546487e19e8a5e6084f06c0a1d8c4d6d5f95d37d1a96f789", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "47dd4c27-d93b-4d5d-9e90-cbad4901c032", "text": "Subtitle in Museo 700 sentence case in Salmon\n\nPage subhead in sentence case Museo 500 in Salmon\n\nBody copy in Museo 100 sentence case in Gray. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:4186f6f5-9922-4626-a7d4-1795188152a9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 180, "token_count": 125, "page_number": 77, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "22871919-5050-4ac5-ad6f-3e7ac5323e58", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "f01f8df9d6d766c0224292fbafd2f2019f26b46ff762395351bab78e0d216f52", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "4186f6f5-9922-4626-a7d4-1795188152a9", "text": "The clinical trial visual assets for OFEV ® are designed, managed, and used in promotional materials in a recognizable way, as established by our Clinical Trial Visual Identity System. The system helps to unify our materials, creating a consistent, flexible, and ownable visual communication style that is maintained across all channels.\n\nDeveloping a strong and consistent link between strategic and design elements is essential to the overall success and recognition of study-related communications."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5829d303-a218-4ef2-803d-81c4e0aabdcd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 181, "token_count": 98, "page_number": 78, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "280ae365-b37a-47f3-a039-1b441d0ab689", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "71253bd666809651b0b91e1893bb48ea73a8e58191e1b3fb32e3cbe249f8328e", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "5829d303-a218-4ef2-803d-81c4e0aabdcd", "text": "The following pages provide details on use of the clinical trial identity assets for OFEV ® . These assets have been created for use in study-related communications; clear direction is provided for utilizing visual elements.\n\nThis section will guide you on how to utilize the unbranded elements, including color palette, typography, templates, and grid systems. Follow these guidelines closely."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:8ff7ee90-d9d1-4f12-bc98-0235599a6fa1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 182, "token_count": 66, "page_number": 79, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "56af75fc-c480-4feb-8350-7b48c6c65c02", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "62217f862eb8f99f2e797e96510167985adb41216fa36bbad3682ad090374d31", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "8ff7ee90-d9d1-4f12-bc98-0235599a6fa1", "text": "Our clinical trial logo consists of 2 elements: the trial name and the symbol. The symbol depicts a hummingbird, representing vigor and energy. The dark blue, all-caps typeface in the trial name communicates innovation and intelligence.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ntriAL nAME"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:d3acfb71-7fb6-47fd-9399-68306ec06582", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 183, "token_count": 54, "page_number": 80, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "971ba75f-0ca6-4f47-aefe-3f2045e45250", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "5cf4fd4cecd68d72781805523700c78dc9d780c803f14ad3f7c01f903e51ab5b", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "d3acfb71-7fb6-47fd-9399-68306ec06582", "text": "There are 6 individual clinical trial names, each with its own logo. These assets are available for download.\n\nLoGo FAMiLY\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:664c258a-a5d1-430e-96b7-f91eeb448bea", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 184, "token_count": 159, "page_number": 81, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "309b47f4-7d60-44d0-ac8c-35905423838e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "d9af25c7807c6891abe2c7903739ac5d505141ce850e24758a77f06c54ae92a9", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "664c258a-a5d1-430e-96b7-f91eeb448bea", "text": "Clear space is the recommended area of white or an empty space surrounding the INPULSIS ® -1 logo. 100% of the cap height of the logotype is equal to 1x. A minimum clear space of 1x should be maintained around the entire mark at all times.\n\nMinimum size is the smallest size at which our brandmark can be reproduced. The minimum size of the INPULSIS ® -1 brandmark is 7/8' (22mm) in width for print and 125 pixels in width for digital applications. For legibility reasons, the brandmark should never be smaller than that.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncLEAr SPAcE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nMiniMuM SizE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPrint: 7/8' (22 mm) diGitAL: 125 PixELS"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:3f930efe-bd30-4d39-88a1-ddfab7c39a42", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 185, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 82, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "060c2da0-9926-4dd5-84bb-fa1856696ccf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "cc6f2aa507f6a1f7de2db7e09ddef04282962c09cb6c6d659f0fa9aa07ac3b6c", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "3f930efe-bd30-4d39-88a1-ddfab7c39a42", "text": "8.5"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:4c7beca7-9f1f-44f4-afbd-6b1946a314a1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 186, "token_count": 161, "page_number": 82, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6a3f0f49-45f8-4651-8367-36706164a224", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "c7ac7dfbb14b51ecc174456e73932da0983f4e8a8942bf948d809c77215d29ee", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "4c7beca7-9f1f-44f4-afbd-6b1946a314a1", "text": "The preferred use of the INPULSIS ® -1 logo is the CMYK version on white background.\n\nThe CMYK and PMS logos are used when printing communication pieces. When printing in black and white, use the grayscale version of the logo. The RGB version of the logo is used for design pieces intended for electronic use such as interfaces, websites, and PowerPoint documents.\n\ncMYK\n\n(PrEFErrEd For ALL PrintEd coMMunicAtionS)\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n(uSEd WHEn SPot coLor PrintinG iS\n\n4 PMS tHE onLY oPtion AVAiLABLE)\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nrGB\n\n(uSEd For diGitAL APPLicAtionS)\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nGrAYScALE (uSEd WHEn FuLL-coLor PrintinG iS not AVAiLABLE)\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:d62086e2-8718-454c-99ee-aed73d15aa38", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 187, "token_count": 230, "page_number": 83, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "48ecd0e5-8bf0-430c-824b-9214a8537f37", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "7bc3d9f3c759971db6ec14929d6522a782964bf7a353d3e1117a3763b73b9fd8", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "d62086e2-8718-454c-99ee-aed73d15aa38", "text": "It can be easy to misuse our logo when implementing across marketing materials.\n\nFor your reference, here are some ways our logo should not be used.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ndo not ALtEr or SWAP AnY oF tHE LoGo'S coLorS\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ndo not crEAtE outLinEd VErSionS oF tHE LoGo\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ndo not rotAtE tHE LoGo\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ndo not iLLuStrAtE tHE LoGo\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ndo not StrEtcH or SKEW tHE LoGo\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ndo not Add droP SHAdoWS to tHE LoGo\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nLorem ipsum dolor                     consectetur adipiscing elit. Vestibulum pellentesque risus pulvinar mauris suscipit volutpat. Duis eleifend quam nibh, in pharetra lorem dapibus.\n\ndo not uSE tHE LoGo in coPY\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ndo not ModiFY or crEAtE nEW LoGotYPE/SYMBoL LocKuPS\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nINPULSIS-1\n\ndo not ModiFY or rEcrEAtE tHE LoGotYPE\n\ndo not PLAcE tHE LoGo on BAcKGroundS tHAt do not ProVidE SuFFiciEnt contrASt\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:5fbf64a5-39f8-4829-afb1-c38ad7a66dd5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 188, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 84, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "5c1cbb75-11ae-4d04-8984-08df19b97060", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "8719c8b9d63c644df3a5b778698dbdaa3c3f1b746f3cbb41b28a5f79a8989229", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "5fbf64a5-39f8-4829-afb1-c38ad7a66dd5", "text": "8.7"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:64d7bef9-1954-4573-a53c-224b76707b04", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 135, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 51, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6b6d27b0-51e0-42a4-b002-6778a38ceef6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "f54f1e8b9a3810596ef045f25d69c96911a0f3bf616071e97262ed9c55462aff", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "64d7bef9-1954-4573-a53c-224b76707b04", "text": "5.3"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:6c891c2c-0127-43f5-9f00-bffbf13ea981", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 190, "token_count": 178, "page_number": 85, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "beaac254-f209-4cd1-887a-843966bcfb18", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "7e9a23494a725624da2b641eefc8144851ebb5e0a27eeb153661326451ed2f8b", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "6c891c2c-0127-43f5-9f00-bffbf13ea981", "text": "The clinical trial colors are the same as our brand colors. They should be used to help maintain brand recognition and impact, and to establish a visual link between the brand and the clinical trials.\n\nIn this color palette, Inspiring Yellow and Brilliant Gold are the primary colors and should be the most prominent colors in the color palette.\n\nGuardian Blue is a secondary color and Premium Orange may be used for highlights in applications as well as in typographical call-outs and subheads.\n\nComfort Gray is included again as a neutral tertiary color that helps balance the palette. Comfort Gray can be used in clinical and scientific situations such as charts or to represent placebo.\n\nINPULSIS COLOR PALETTE"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:c01ddf10-ab34-48f6-8acd-04699f5c7aad", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 191, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 85, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2e8838a4-9413-4256-9275-b85373ea8aaf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "37d69c8b511ef0a944ae6f9e190126b13d226cc09f3b6b77bc2a7d1143b0d728", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "c01ddf10-ab34-48f6-8acd-04699f5c7aad", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\nPMS Orange 021"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:7a93dac4-9a68-4830-aeff-33f2e9c132ca", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 192, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 86, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "885a58fd-e3b8-4791-bf34-66c0e061024c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "ed151875c927e3d17c7042cc970f3ea839b03adf00173612f54e39cb0fdf9d04", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "7a93dac4-9a68-4830-aeff-33f2e9c132ca", "text": "8.9"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:ce48a9ed-8c5d-4c57-b053-e0d1e6035b56", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 193, "token_count": 64, "page_number": 86, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3379ee4f-b2e1-4db9-8e67-7a79ea26d2c5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "8c2210faba01868f26204f81a1988da4b80f385edf233d11ebed89d217af9a60", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "ce48a9ed-8c5d-4c57-b053-e0d1e6035b56", "text": "Clinical trial visual identity assets include more than just color and typography. The secondary graphics for the clinical trials provide an ownable and recognizable look-beyond the logo-that can be used on all study-related communications.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:d8534697-6adc-4605-b9e0-01dbcd22097e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 194, "token_count": 96, "page_number": 87, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "76eba09f-7bc3-4db1-a3c1-f29d47d0686b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "10619a0b2305c7edd9232fec2563505aa2a9cfe233d2d94541a52d4c89f364a7", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "d8534697-6adc-4605-b9e0-01dbcd22097e", "text": "Our secondary graphics have been designed to accommodate a variety of layouts and content. The size of the shapes can be scaled up, down, and sideways, adding flexibility to the system while maintaining a consistent look.\n\nBlue should always be the dominant color on the page; the golden supergraphic should be used as a secondary element.\n\noFEV\\_HorizontAL\\_cMYK.Ai\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:acdcfc77-a332-4305-8663-905db766ac16", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 195, "token_count": 78, "page_number": 88, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "1e45624e-d809-4909-a45f-11c6fffa514e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "87c386c69b6f4eaf13fc568a3a43dacf1625d79bc5e840dcc2c724feb299ef06", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "acdcfc77-a332-4305-8663-905db766ac16", "text": "The key elements of the clinical trial materials are the secondary graphics (the dominant blue color and the golden supergraphic), the clinical trial logo, and the written content. These elements complement one another and work synergistically to communicate in a clear and compelling way.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n.\n\nY"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:f2fdba14-ada4-4dd4-a88b-4ca0821a5311", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 196, "token_count": 28, "page_number": 89, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0d081977-3ef6-4372-b0c2-b6b43442bfaf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "bf065cf158d4ed254807d7ac85ba4faa33a59461ebf08874ee425b386852c13f", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "f2fdba14-ada4-4dd4-a88b-4ca0821a5311", "text": "PowerPoint templates enable us to present information with clarity, credibility, and consistency.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:2f1aceeb-7d67-41b1-b87e-86c25a6d9359", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 197, "token_count": 20, "page_number": 90, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "956e02af-78dd-45f6-8188-fe1db695eedc", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "912a01d557f07267762d2f5dd9f07abcb484373bf1754eaec94b57220b0c0ebb", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "2f1aceeb-7d67-41b1-b87e-86c25a6d9359", "text": "Illustrated to the right is an example of a clinical trial folder.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:1fc87fa1-4b41-4475-817a-d19395b696f5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 198, "token_count": 25, "page_number": 91, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "60372b10-c191-4cde-a264-df5ed6c6198f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "a0835d0f703912fca839cfa48eb523cbd14228d0f155c5fbef5afa86c6c27a40", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "1fc87fa1-4b41-4475-817a-d19395b696f5", "text": "The letterhead to the right demonstrates use of the clinical trial stationery system.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:b18da0fb-d74f-4f3b-8356-d03b1dc296e4", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 199, "token_count": 16, "page_number": 92, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "5463938d-d6a7-442b-bfff-a7e6d4c8c760", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "817608aeb4472447eb5365837c82d0060bda320da2f217eeb9db8824a4da7d19", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "b18da0fb-d74f-4f3b-8356-d03b1dc296e4", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:8b5c72b6-823d-45ab-9107-a0a7c8b90c6f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 200, "token_count": 55, "page_number": 93, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "564892e7-16a6-4e83-99f7-309913fdae70", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "4044471889ccdf5eefae9ccdb4b214927684b7075eaf1c99a9f7b2a58150e5d4", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "8b5c72b6-823d-45ab-9107-a0a7c8b90c6f", "text": "Knowing how to access and use the OFEV ® brand assets is critical for ease in applying them. This section explains the file nomenclature and provides assets for download, contact information, and a quick reference guide."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:d4d5fbfa-6b11-45af-a23c-39af0fef430d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 201, "token_count": 144, "page_number": 94, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "85a8ee51-9331-49ce-9d98-b4ae48e70509", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "c205a65d18b3aa2628d61a9eb945af88402ff7120b7bee1123688979edf43bdd", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "d4d5fbfa-6b11-45af-a23c-39af0fef430d", "text": "Please refer to the document entitled Overview of IPF Materials (ID number in BI Vault: 000). It lists all of the branded and unbranded campaign tactics prepared by the corporate marketing team. These tactics are meant to be translated and adapted for use in your local market. Use the identification numbers in this document to locate and download the tactics. A PDF of each tactic is accompanied by a literature pack as well as a ZIP file containing the art files; your agency can use these materials to customize the tactic and prepare for regulatory review.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:c0f70cf6-36f5-4363-bffc-f5471dc107bb", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 202, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 95, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "29f4a2ae-c22a-424d-a02a-706e1975fe9b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "cbcc2089e2e9234a1b3800dd05d06511d356404e85a23a4a8b4bec2fc3d65a38", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "c0f70cf6-36f5-4363-bffc-f5471dc107bb", "text": "9.2"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:35b24151-9162-49fa-8cd6-34add4bf74fc", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 203, "token_count": 218, "page_number": 95, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "89202da0-0ccd-4f15-acee-1666d4e198de", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "cefb0794c7da6cae8bcdecb0409586557115d838047c755089bbec4f223bb293", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "35b24151-9162-49fa-8cd6-34add4bf74fc", "text": "The following nomenclature system has been developed to help identify and easily locate the various graphic files. Please always use the downloadable electronic reproducible art we have provided.\n\nThe various file formats available are: AI (Adobe Illustrator) files are used for all high-quality printing. These files are in a vector format and can be scaled up or down without loss of quality.\n\nJPG (Joint Photographic Experts Group) files are in a compressed format best used on the Internet because they are in RGB. They cannot be scaled up without loss of quality.\n\nPNG (Portable Network Graphics) files are used for importing artwork into PowerPoint for on-screen presentations. These files can also be used on the Internet. This is a compressed format; files are best created at full size and not scaled up or down. PNG files are created with a transparent background."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:775be542-d4d8-42df-bc61-06fac07820fe", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 92, "token_count": 83, "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e0db6756-7ed7-4ae1-a3c8-8e4785d86090", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "e22541cdcdb25b01fd79a58b68df3e861c92f91498b0ad9853e253c02d516e90", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "775be542-d4d8-42df-bc61-06fac07820fe", "text": "A clear space should be maintained around the Boehringer Ingelheim logo with dimensions equal to the diameter of the Boehringer Ingelheim symbol.\n\nThe logo lockup has a standard height of 12 mm and should be no less than 6 mm.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncLEAr SPAcE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nMiniMuM SizE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nStAndArd SizE\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:98b857f8-9bcd-4e91-9a53-751ba0f44b1b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 204, "token_count": 162, "page_number": 95, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "94ef50bb-4c16-4fd6-8098-b08e1bd5e6b1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "3a2fbcaabd9fe69c4a77f717d280c821be8d4d15b40c80f300532214fb5b2138", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "98b857f8-9bcd-4e91-9a53-751ba0f44b1b", "text": "Product Name\n\nOFEV OFEV ®  (nintedanib)\n\n| Type of Asset L Logo   | TAG Tagline US United States GLOBAL Global PURE No Tagline SYMBOL Symbol Only   | Positive/ Negative/ Graphic Color Type P Positive N Negative   | Color Mode 3PMS 3 Pantone Spot Color CMYK 4-Color Process RGB Digital Publishing GS Grayscale   | Extension .ai .jpg .pdf .png   |\n|------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:a198018d-d669-420f-9587-881a74664b8d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 205, "token_count": 218, "page_number": 96, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "968357fa-6ef8-422f-9dba-15bf92f4b8cb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "cefb0794c7da6cae8bcdecb0409586557115d838047c755089bbec4f223bb293", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "a198018d-d669-420f-9587-881a74664b8d", "text": "The following nomenclature system has been developed to help identify and easily locate the various graphic files. Please always use the downloadable electronic reproducible art we have provided.\n\nThe various file formats available are: AI (Adobe Illustrator) files are used for all high-quality printing. These files are in a vector format and can be scaled up or down without loss of quality.\n\nJPG (Joint Photographic Experts Group) files are in a compressed format best used on the Internet because they are in RGB. They cannot be scaled up without loss of quality.\n\nPNG (Portable Network Graphics) files are used for importing artwork into PowerPoint for on-screen presentations. These files can also be used on the Internet. This is a compressed format; files are best created at full size and not scaled up or down. PNG files are created with a transparent background."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:ofev:chunk:232f8e36-ce5e-42fd-8b1c-b3adadec39f0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 206, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 96, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ecef8a2b-9330-4beb-9d70-00653a90b973", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf", "source_hash": "faa3412c25b55f10fcce06f5e39e18fc694ac46ce398482016249451af600403", "source_document_id": "7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2", "chunk_id": "232f8e36-ce5e-42fd-8b1c-b3adadec39f0", "text": "| US                   |\n|----------------------|\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_3PMS.ai  |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_cMYK.ai  |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_GS.ai    |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_rGB.ai   |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_3PMS.jpg |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_cMYK.jpg |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_GS.jpg   |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_rGB.jpg  |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_3PMS.pdf |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_cMYK.pdf |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_GS.pdf   |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_rGB.pdf  |\n| oFEV_L_uS_P_rGB.png  |\n\n| Global With Tagline   |\n|-----------------------|\n